  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the variances of the lotteries and choosing the one with lower variance. However, the individual did not mention or imply any consideration of variance, spread, or risk beyond noting that the probabilities of winning are similar. Instead, the individual’s justification centers on preferring a higher payoff when the chances are nearly equal. There is no alignment between the information used by the individual (win amount and its probability) and the information required by the decision reason (full variance calculation). Furthermore, the individual’s rule (choose higher payoff when probabilities are similar) differs from the reason’s rule (choose lower variance). Therefore, there is no evidence the individual used variance as a criterion.",
